      "id": 1,
      "text": "Melvin began in 1862 as a single saloon that drew travelers enough to spark a growing settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://99wfmk.com/melvin-michigan/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By 1884 the village boasted a church, depot, drug store, general store, grocery, grist mill, hotel, post office, saloon, and sawmill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://99wfmk.com/melvin-michigan/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Port Huron & Northwestern Railroad arrived in the late 1800s, turning Melvin into a railway stop and postal station in 1874.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://99wfmk.com/melvin-michigan/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The original First Baptist Church, still standing today, was co‑built by William Clayton Roof and sits beside a historic cemetery.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
